meta {
	name: ResourceRequestRightKeysV2
	seq: 11
}

auth {
	mode: inherit
}

docs {
	# Resource requests with selected rights (right keys), API version 2

	BDD scenarios for the version 2 end user request endpoints under
	`/accessmanagement/api/v2/enduser/request`, where a resource request can name the rights it
	asks for and the approver can choose which rights to give (#4604, #4605). They double as
	usage documentation: every request carries a `docs` block with what the endpoint does, the
	parameters it takes and the response it returns.

	Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
	`NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. A scenario starts from a known
	state, removes what it created, and can run standalone or repeatedly.

	## Endpoints

	- `POST v2/enduser/request/resource`: create a resource request, optionally with
		`{ "requestedRightKeys": [...] }`.
	- `PUT v2/enduser/request/received/approve`: approve, optionally with
		`{ "rightKeys": [...] }` selecting the rights to give. The status becomes Approved or
		PartialApprove.
	- `GET v2/enduser/request`, `sent` and `received`: the v2 request, with `status` as a
		non-exhaustive string and the keys in `resource.requestedRightKeys` and
		`resource.approvedRightKeys`.
	- Version 1 of the same endpoints reports PartialApprove as `status` Approved with
		`statusV2` PartialApprove, leaves the right keys out, and sends a `Deprecation` header and
		a `successor-version` link to version 2.

	Right keys are opaque hashes from the resource policy. The scenarios look them up through
	`GET v1/enduser/connections/resources/delegationcheck` instead of hard-coding them.

	## Feature flags

	`AccessManagement.Enduser.RequestV2Api` and `AccessMgmt.Controller.RequestAssignment.Resource`
	must be on in the target environment. With the first off, every v2 call returns 404.
	The Azure DevOps post-deployment run executes the whole `test` folder in every environment,
	so every step starts with `skipOutsideEnabledEnvironments()` from `helpers.js`, which skips
	the request outside `enabledEnvironments` before the step loads seed data. TT02 has seed
	data, but stays out of the list until the flag is on there.

	## Tokens and fixtures

	Personas live in `testdata/delegationrequest-scenarios/<tokenEnv>.js` under
	`resourceRequestRightKeysV2`, and come from the `be-om-tilgang` fixtures:

	- `requester`: an organisation asking for access, acting through its innehaver.
	- `approver`: a private person, connected to the requester, asked to grant access.
	- `resource`: a ttd resource on which the approver can delegate at least two rights.

	Every step mints a personal token with the scope `altinn:portal/enduser` through
	`helpers.js`. Requests cannot be deleted, so each scenario rejects stale pending requests
	in its GIVEN step and removes the delegation it created in its CLEANUP step.

	The v1 suite in `Resource_DelegationRequest` uses the same pair and resource; the GIVEN
	steps reset what it leaves behind.
}
